Z||000000||Phoenix||10-10-2000||12:29 PM||||I've searched all the topic but couldn't find an answer - so here goes.  Are the struts for all years the same? shockwarehouse.com doesn't list a KYB for 88 but they do for 84-87's.  The Fiero store list the same KYB for all years.  BTW - Shockwarehouse has good prices and they shipped the front shocks to me the same day as I ordered them.<P>TIA||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||10-10-2000||04:12 PM||||Pontiac changed the suspension for 1988.  Best suspension available..limited production year..no suspension parts available for the 88.  I had all the struts replaced at Mr. Goodwrench with GM replacement parts two years ago.  I think the 88s struts are different than previous years.  Call the Fiero Store to confirm or maybe Fiero Dave, Orgre or one of the other experts who do their own repairs knows the answer.||||reg||3
Z||000002||Pontiaddict||10-10-2000||06:53 PM||||I think production struts were valved differently for 88s. KYBs would be valved differently from stock so it wouldn't matter what year thay were on. <P>Don't quote me on that though.||||reg||1
